// Client-safe Supabase config, committed (not gitignored) deliberately. GT_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
// is Supabase's "publishable" key -- their own dashboard labels it safe to share publicly,
// and the real security boundary is Row Level Security on the database (see DECISIONS.md /
// KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md), not keeping this value secret. GT_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF isn't
// sensitive either. Stored as a bare ref rather than a full https:// URL because xcconfig
// treats "//" as a comment marker even inside a value -- SupabaseAuthAdapter builds the full
// URL from this at runtime.
//
// The service_role/secret key never appears here, or anywhere under ios/ -- it stays in the
// root .env (gitignored) and, later, GitHub Actions secrets for Edge Function deployment only.
//
// These two values are ALSO duplicated as literals directly in project.yml's
// INFOPLIST_KEY_GTSupabaseProjectRef/INFOPLIST_KEY_GTSupabaseAnonKey settings (not referenced
// via $(GT_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF)-style substitution from here) -- a real crash on the first
// real device launch traced to that substitution never actually reaching the compiled
// Info.plist. Update BOTH files if these values ever change. See DECISIONS.md.

GT_SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF = wraowtlpekpmpekkcquq
GT_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = sb_publishable_DbHsYI9HsdbqQ4rUM0Lb_w_bdi25XpF
